From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 07:32:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(llama-cpp): the encoder output of an encoder-decoder
 model is kept per sequence

On top of the encoder-decoder support (patches/0003) and the waves
(patches/0004): T5 gets its own memory (llama_memory_enc_dec), the
decoder's KV cache plus the encoder outputs per sequence, so a slot is
encoded while others decode and a late request joins the next decode step
instead of waiting for the wave. A sequence without an encoder output is
refused (-1), never asserted on. No public API changes; only T5 reaches
the new code. Carried as a llama.cpp patch beside the others
(patches/0006-encoder-decoder-memory.patch).

Checked on the CPU with a random-weight T5: the library tests (a lone
sequence bitwise equal to a one-sequence context, two sequences in one
batch within nmse 1e-4 of their solo runs, removals and state), and the
0004 server checks (byte-identical to 0003 alone, the same 7 prompts in 3
orders, bursts).

Assisted-by: Claude Code
